{{!
    @template block_download_certificates/zip_form

    A ZIP request: a POST form to one of the plugin's download pages, with the session key in its
    body. Used by the block and by the pages' header.

    Data attributes required for JS (async_download.js):
    * data-download-type - The request type.
    * data-cert-count - The certificates the request holds.
    * data-async-threshold - From this count on, the request is queued in the background.
    * data-confirm - The question asked before the request goes, when there is one.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * url - The download page.
    * type, count, threshold - As the data attributes above.
    * sesskey - The session key.
    * fields - The hidden fields: name, value.
    * label - The button text.
    * buttonclass - The button's classes besides btn.
    * confirm - The question, or false.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "url": "https://example.com/blocks/download_certificates/download.php",
        "type": "all",
        "count": 42,
        "threshold": 30,
        "sesskey": "abc123",
        "fields": [
            {"name": "action", "value": "download_all"}
        ],
        "label": "Download all",
        "buttonclass": "btn-success btn-sm w-100",
        "confirm": "Are you sure you want to download all certificates?"
    }
}}
<form method="post" action="{{url}}" class="block-download-certificates-zip mb-2"
      data-download-type="{{type}}" data-cert-count="{{count}}" data-async-threshold="{{threshold}}"
      {{#confirm}}data-confirm="{{.}}"{{/confirm}}>
    <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
    {{#fields}}
    <input type="hidden" name="{{name}}" value="{{value}}">
    {{/fields}}
    <button type="submit" class="btn {{buttonclass}}">
        <i class="fa fa-download me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{label}}
    </button>
</form>
